## 1. Data

The dataset is the ULB *Credit Card Fraud Detection* table: ${n_rows} transactions in ${n_columns} columns
(`Time`, `V1`–`V28`, `Amount`, `Class`). `V1`–`V28` are anonymised numerical features, `Time` is the number of seconds since the first
transaction, `Class` is 1 for fraud. The file spans ${time_span_hours} hours and contains ${n_fraud} frauds, i.e. ${fraud_rate} % of the rows
(about ${imbalance_ratio} legitimate transactions per fraud), so plain accuracy is not informative and the project uses PR-AUC,
recall at a fixed precision and threshold tuning.

The official source is Kaggle (`mlg-ulb/creditcardfraud`, login required). To keep the project reproducible without a login, the same file is
downloaded from a public mirror (`src/data/download.py`) and verified: header, ${n_rows} rows and ${n_fraud} frauds must match.
SHA-256 of the file used: `${sha256}`.

